DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The kkllddnneexxtt() system call returns the fileid of the next kld file (that
     is, the one after _f_i_l_e_i_d) or 0 if _f_i_l_e_i_d is the last file loaded.  To get
     the fileid of the first kld file, pass _f_i_l_e_i_d of 0 to kkllddnneexxtt().

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The kkllddnneexxtt() system call returns the fileid of the next kld file or 0 if
     successful.  Otherwise kkllddnneexxtt() returns the value -1 and sets the global
     variable _e_r_r_n_o to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The only error set by kkllddnneexxtt() is ENOENT, which is set when _f_i_l_e_i_d
     refers to a kld file that does not exist (is not loaded).

